course: dictionary
lesson: 7310
title: Pixels: the tiny dots that make pictures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pixel is one tiny coloured dot in a picture. Zoom in very close to a screen or a digital photo and you will see a grid of these dots, like a mosaic made of tiny tiles. «A digital picture is a grid of tiny coloured squares called pixels.» Each square is one pixel.
explain: Pixels are also a way to measure size. «1,920 pixels wide» tells you how many dots fit across a screen from one side to the other. More pixels means more dots, so the picture can show more detail and look sharper.
explain: Each pixel can show many colours. «Each pixel has a red, a green and a blue part that glow a little or a lot, and mixing those three makes every colour you see.» So a yellow banana and a purple dragon are both made from the same three colours of light, mixed in different amounts.
fact: A pixel is one tiny dot of a digital picture.
fact: A digital picture is a grid of tiny coloured squares called pixels.
fact: Each pixel's colour is stored as numbers for how much red, green and blue it has (RGB).
fact: «Pixelated» means a picture looks blocky, because you can see the separate pixels.
fact: «Digital zoom» just enlarges pixels and loses detail; a real zoom lens gives sharper pictures.
exercise: «A digital picture is a grid of tiny coloured squares called pixels.» What is a pixel? | A kind of camera lens | *One tiny coloured dot or square that makes up a picture | The name of a computer game | A large window on a wall
exercise: A coin falls 2, then 4, then 6 pixels in three frames. How many pixels has it fallen in total? | *12 | 3 | 18 | 8
exercise: «1,920 pixels wide» tells you about a screen. What does this measure? | *How wide the screen is, counted in pixels | How heavy the screen is | How many people can see it | How fast the screen turns on
test: «Each pixel has a red, a green and a blue part.» Why can a screen show a purple dragon? | It only has purple pixels | *Its pixels mix red, green and blue light in different amounts | Screens cannot show purple | Each pixel is a tiny dragon
test: A picture is 10 pixels wide and 10 pixels high. How many pixels does it have altogether? | 20 | *100 | 10 | 1,000
exam: Which statement about pixels is true? | Digital zoom adds new pixels that make the picture sharper | Pixels are only used for measuring time | A pixel is a whole picture on a screen | *Pixels are tiny dots that make up a picture, and more of them means sharper detail
